---------------------------------------------- Router quiz -----------------------------------------

- Let's check your knowledge of the router!


1️⃣ Which of the following route declarations are valid?

        { path: '/', component: Home }

        { path: '', component: Home }   ✅

        { path: '', component: Home, canActivate: [AuthGuard] } ✅

        { path: '', outlet: Home }



2️⃣ How do you initialize the router in your application?

        imports: [provideRouterModule(routes)]

        providers: [provideRouterModule(routes)]

        providers: [provideRouter(routes)]  ✅



3️⃣ What types of guard can be used? (see section 7)

        CanActivate ✅

        CanMatch    ✅

        CanAuthenticate

        CanDeactivate   ✅



4️⃣ How can you access a route param called id and store it in a signal of the component? (see section 3)

        this.id.set(route.snapshot.id)

        this.id.set(route.snapshot.paramMap.get('id'))  ✅

        this.id = toSignal(route.paramMap.pipe(map(params => params.get('id')))) ✅



5️⃣ How can you add a link to the Races page in the template? (see section 3)

        <a routerLink="/races"> ✅

        <a href="races">

        <a [routerLink]="['/races']"    ✅



6️⃣ How can you navigate to the Races page from the code? (see section 3)

        router.navigate(['/races']) ✅

        router.goTo('/races')

        router.navigateByUrl('/races')  ✅